On 02/05/2013 07:22 AM, Alexander Beaujean wrote:
> Can you give a reference (or link, etc.) for how lavaan estimates the
> residual variances in the 'delta' parameterization? I had assumed they
> were set to one.

One reference is:

Muth�n, B. (1978). Contributions to factor analysis of dichotomous
variables. Psychometrika, 43, 551-560.
(www.statmodel.com/download/ContributionsToFactorAnalysis.pdf <http://www.statmodel.com/download/ContributionsToFactorAnalysis.pdf>)

Equation 4 (page 554) shows how the (diagonal) elements of 'Psi'
(corresponding with the residual variances of the observed variables)
are a function of other model parameters.

Yves.

